{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U5", "NAVCPeripherals"],
      "pins": ["U5.7"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "GND"],
      "observed": "BMI088 pin 7 (PS, protocol select) is on the +3.3V net, not on GND. The GND net only contains U5 pins 4 and 6.",
      "expected": "For I2C operation, as the spec requires (BMI088 at I2C addresses 0x19 and 0x69), the BMI088 PS pin should be tied low (GND). Tying it high selects SPI, so the sensor would not respond on the I2C bus at those addresses.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PS\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GNDA\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Bosch BMI088, I2C addr 0x19 (acc) / 0x69 (gyr)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The IMU would likely not respond on I2C, so the navigation computer would lose accelerometer and gyro data.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["REG1", "R60", "C6", "D1"],
      "pins": ["REG1.20", "R60.2", "D1.1"],
      "nets": ["REG_BST", "REG_CS"],
      "observed": "The BST net contains only D1 cathode, R60 pin 2 and REG1 pin 20. There is no capacitor between BST and SW. R60 (10 Ω) sits between the SW node and BST in that position instead.",
      "expected": "The MIC26903 needs a bootstrap capacitor (typically 100 nF) between BST and SW, fed from the VDD diode D1. A 10 Ω resistor in that path cannot store charge for the high-side gate drive.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"118\") (name \"REG_BST\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R60\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"REG1\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"BST\") (pintype \"unspecified\")))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R60 REG_CS REG_BST 10"}
      ],
      "impact": "The high-side switch of the 5 V buck converter may not drive correctly, so the 5 V rail may fail to regulate or may run erratically, which would starve the servo bank and the logic supplies.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "I2C2_SCL_FCC", "I2C2_SDA_FCC"],
      "observed": "PCA9685 A0 (pin 1) is tied to +3.3V, while A1 through A5 are on GND. This gives an I2C address of 0x41 rather than the specified 0x40.",
      "expected": "The spec gives the PCA9685PW address as 0x40, which requires A0 to be low (GND).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A0\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"}
      ],
      "impact": "The flight controller may fail to address the PWM driver at 0x40, so the servo outputs would not be updated. This may have been a deliberate choice to avoid a clash with the INA219 at 0x40 on the same bus, so it is a lower-confidence finding.",
      "confidence": 0.25
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows the BMI088 PS pin tied high, which conflicts with the I2C operation the spec requires, and the 5 V buck's bootstrap path has a 10 Ω resistor where a bootstrap capacitor should be. The PCA9685 A0 strap also differs from the stated 0x40 address. Most MCU pin connectivity is absent from this export, so I did not treat those gaps as anomalies."
}

